hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2856","I read to Ahmad bin Abi Suraig ar-Razi that Amr bin Mujammic informed them, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn Umar (RA), who said: \"When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was mounted on his mount at the Masjid of Dhu al-Hulayfah, he would pronounce the Talbiyah (Ihram).\" He mentioned the rest of the hadith and said: \"He would spend the night (at Muzdalifah"
